title: 26 September
subtitle: Passive resistance ends, and the Reich comes under emergency rule.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1923 and month >= 9 and e23_sept_done = 0 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
priority: 2
on-arrival: {!
RG.news('Passive resistance ends: a state of emergency for the Reich', 3);
Q.e23_sept_done = 1;
Q.repression += 6;
Q.army_loyalty += 4;
Q.inflation = Math.min(100, Q.inflation + 6);
!}

= 26 September

On 26 September [+ chancellor +] announces the end of passive resistance in the Ruhr. The Reich can no longer pay for it: the dollar costs a hundred and sixty million marks. [? if bavaria_soviet != 2 : The same day Bavaria makes Gustav von Kahr General State Commissioner with dictatorial powers, and the Reichswehr division in Munich takes his side against Berlin. ?][? if bavaria_soviet = 2 : The nationalist leagues demand that the Reich march on Red Bavaria at last. ?]

That night Ebert declares a state of emergency for the whole Reich. Executive power passes to the Reichswehr minister, which means to General von Seeckt and his district commanders. In Saxony and Thuringia General Müller and General Reinhardt are now the real governments. [? if e23_october_done = 1 : The decree was drafted with our rising of the summer in mind. ?]

- @protest: Call a protest strike in Saxony.
- @prepare: Say little, and move the rifles to Saxony.

@protest
subtitle: A show of strength, and a list of names for the generals.
view-if: offensive_gone = 0 or ultraleft_gone = 0
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike('saxony');
RG.district('saxony', {repression: 8, militancy: 6});
Q.lean_offensive += 1;
!}

The protest strike is solid in Saxony and patchy in Berlin. The next day the military commanders ban our papers in four districts.

@prepare
subtitle: Better armed where it may matter. Berlin is left thinner.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district('saxony', {guards: 2});
RG.district('thuringia', {guards: 1});
RG.district('berlin', {guards: -0.5});
Q.red_guards_arms += 4;
!}

Lorries with crates marked "machine parts" drive by night from Berlin and Halle to Chemnitz and Zwickau.
